          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[#333333] text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,17px)]">Q1: What is an active harmonic filter (AHF)?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[#626469] text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,17px)] leading-relaxed">An active harmonic filter is a power-electronics device that measures the load current with an external CT, isolates the harmonic, reactive and imbalance components with a DSP, and injects an equal and opposite compensation current through an IGBT inverter bridge. The utility then sees a clean fundamental waveform.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-border-light p-5">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[#333333] text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,17px)]">Q2: How does the AHF work?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[#626469] text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,17px)] leading-relaxed">An external CT samples the load current; a DSP/FPGA runs an FFT to separate 2nd–51st order harmonics, reactive power and imbalance; the IGBT inverter bridge then injects an equal and opposite-phase compensation current. The result is THDi held below 5% per IEEE 519 at the point of common coupling.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-border-light p-5">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[#333333] text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,17px)]">Q3: What capacity and voltage range is available?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[#626469] text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,17px)] leading-relaxed">8 A – 20 A per module (parallel expandable, unlimited), 3P3W/3P4W, covering 208–690V. Modules parallel without a practical limit to reach 3000 A and beyond for large plants.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-border-light p-5">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[#333333] text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,17px)]">Q4: Can it also correct power factor and balance loads?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[#626469] text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,17px)] leading-relaxed">Yes. A selectable priority function covers harmonic mitigation, reactive compensation and three-phase balancing. In 3P4W mode it also cancels the accumulated 3rd-harmonic neutral current.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-border-light p-5">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[#333333] text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,17px)]">Q5: How is it installed and what protection rating does it have?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[#626469] text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,17px)] leading-relaxed">Installed as wall-mounted or rack / cabinet type; rated IP20, IP30, IP65 (customizable). The enclosure is built for the duty cycle of industrial switchrooms and can be customized for harsher or outdoor sites.</p>
